import GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.MpcGeneralTowerBracketBoundary

/-!
# The reachable-stage tower boundary for the general Mpc argument

The unrestricted head-completion interface asks for absorption at every tuple of group
elements.  The finite-stage induction needs it only at tuples satisfying the uniform stage
equations.  Those equations contain the relator and symplectic information, so retaining them
is essential for the final graded argument.

This file rebuilds the last reduction on that honest state space.  It remains simultaneous in
`alpha`, the handle count, and the filtration rung.  The resulting boundary is one theorem:
at every reachable stage, each canonical tower atom bracket with the current `D` letter lies
in the fully marked correction range.
-/

namespace GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.MpcGeneralStageTowerBoundary

noncomputable section

open GQ2 GQ2.Dyadic Multiplicative
